A **dashboard** application: a React frontend built on
[`design-kit`](https://github.com/hollis-labs/design-kit) and `kit-dashboard` served by a
Go binary through the [`go-webui`](https://github.com/hollis-labs/go-webui)
embed harness. Scaffolded by `folio new app-dashboard`.

## Layout

```
cmd/{{ .inputs.project_name }}/   Go entrypoint — HTTP server + /api
internal/webui/             //go:embed all:dist + the go-webui handler
frontend/                   Vite + React frontend (the dashboard UI)
  src/App.tsx               AppShell — nav rail + page header
  src/pages/                one page per screen
  src/api/                  same-origin API client + typed context
```

The frontend builds into `internal/webui/dist/`, which the Go binary
embeds — so a single binary serves both the API and the UI.

## Prerequisites

- Go {{ .inputs.go_version }}+
- Node.js 20+ / npm

## Develop

Two processes during development:

```sh
make run      # Go server on 127.0.0.1:8080 (serves /api and the last UI build)
make ui-dev   # Vite dev server with hot reload — proxies /api to 127.0.0.1:8080
```

Open the Vite dev server URL — the app is served under
`{{ .inputs.base_path }}/`, not the root path.

## Build a release binary

```sh
make all      # ui-build (vite → internal/webui/dist) then build
./{{ .inputs.project_name }}
```

The dashboard UI is then served at <http://localhost:8080{{ .inputs.base_path }}/>.
Before the first `make ui-build`, `go-webui` serves a "not built"
placeholder in place of the app. The server defaults to `127.0.0.1:8080`.
For containers, set `LISTEN_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8080` explicitly to listen on all
interfaces. Set `LISTEN_ADDR` to choose another address or port; if the port
changes, update the development proxy in `frontend/vite.config.ts` too.

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make ui-build` | Build the frontend into `internal/webui/dist` |
| `make ui-dev` | Run the Vite dev server (hot reload) |
| `make build` | Build the Go binary |
| `make all` | `ui-build` then `build` |
| `make run` | Build and run the server |
| `make install` | Build the embedded UI + install `{{ .inputs.project_name }}` to `$GOBIN` |
| `make test` / `make vet` | Go test / vet |

## Adding a page

A page is generic kit chrome plus app-specific content. Add a component
under `frontend/src/pages/`, then wire it into `frontend/src/App.tsx`
(extend the `nav` array and the active-route switch). Add API endpoints
to `frontend/src/api/client.ts`. See the
[`kit-dashboard` README](https://github.com/hollis-labs/design-kit/tree/main/packages/kit-dashboard)
for the `PageHeader` / `DataTable` / `SummaryCards` composition pattern.

## Dependencies

The design-kit version input defaults to 0.4.0, generating `^0.4.0` ranges.
Tailwind v4 is declared explicitly to satisfy the styled packages' required peer.
Existing generated apps keep their dependencies until intentionally updated.

- **design-kit** (`^{{ .inputs.design_kit_version }}` from npm) — `design-tokens`,
  `design-components` (including AppShell), `design-app-runtime` (API client/context
  and shell reset), and `kit-dashboard` (nav, header, summary and theme).
- **`@hollis-labs/eslint-config-design`** (`^{{ .inputs.design_kit_version }}`) —
  the token contract gate. `npm run lint` runs Biome and this ESLint lane; CI
  typechecks, lints and builds the frontend before compiling the embedded server.
  Components name tokens, never raw colors or scale values. Import base controls
  from `design-components`, app transport from `design-app-runtime`, dashboard
  layout/table/chart surfaces from the matching `kit-dashboard` subpath.
- **`github.com/hollis-labs/go-webui`** (`{{ .inputs.go_webui_version }}`) —
  the SPA-serving harness.

